Split the integral across the three subregions, keeping each integrand attached to its region:

$$
\begin{aligned}
&\iint_{R} f(x,y)\,\mathrm{d}A\\&\quad=\iint_{S} f\,\mathrm{d}A+\iint_{T} f\,\mathrm{d}A+\iint_{U} f\,\mathrm{d}A
\end{aligned}
$$

Substitute the three branches:

$$
\begin{aligned}
&\iint_{R} f(x,y)\,\mathrm{d}A\\&\quad=\iint_{S} (e^{x+y})\,\mathrm{d}A+\iint_{T} (y\cos x)\,\mathrm{d}A\\&\qquad+\iint_{U} (0)\,\mathrm{d}A\\&\quad=\iint_{T} (y\cos x)\,\mathrm{d}A+\iint_{S} (e^{x+y})\,\mathrm{d}A.
\end{aligned}
$$

The contribution on $U$ is zero and disappears.

Split the integral across the three subregions, keeping each integrand attached to its region:

$$
\begin{aligned}
&\iint_{R} f(x,y)\,\mathrm{d}A\\&\quad=\iint_{S} f\,\mathrm{d}A+\iint_{T} f\,\mathrm{d}A+\iint_{U} f\,\mathrm{d}A
\end{aligned}
$$

Substitute the three branches:

$$
\begin{aligned}
&\iint_{R} f(x,y)\,\mathrm{d}A\\&\quad=\iint_{S} (x)\,\mathrm{d}A+\iint_{T} (0)\,\mathrm{d}A\\&\qquad+\iint_{U} (x^{2}y)\,\mathrm{d}A\\&\quad=\iint_{S} (x)\,\mathrm{d}A+\iint_{U} (x^{2}y)\,\mathrm{d}A.
\end{aligned}
$$

The contribution on $T$ is zero and disappears.

Split the integral across the three subregions, keeping each integrand attached to its region:

$$
\begin{aligned}
&\iint_{R} f(x,y)\,\mathrm{d}A\\&\quad=\iint_{S} f\,\mathrm{d}A+\iint_{T} f\,\mathrm{d}A+\iint_{U} f\,\mathrm{d}A
\end{aligned}
$$

Substitute the three branches:

$$
\begin{aligned}
&\iint_{R} f(x,y)\,\mathrm{d}A\\&\quad=\iint_{S} (0)\,\mathrm{d}A+\iint_{T} (2xy^{3})\,\mathrm{d}A\\&\qquad+\iint_{U} (\sqrt[3]{x}y-\sqrt[3]{y})\,\mathrm{d}A\\&\quad=\iint_{U} (\sqrt[3]{x}y-\sqrt[3]{y})\,\mathrm{d}A+\iint_{T} (2xy^{3})\,\mathrm{d}A.
\end{aligned}
$$

The contribution on $S$ is zero and disappears.
